(* The package m5-speaker: tones on the speaker of an M5Stack core, through
   M5Unified. Grades: time-interval-rational, in milliseconds.

   Beep (frequency, duration) starts a tone of the given frequency, in hertz,
   for the given duration, in milliseconds, replacing a tone still playing,
   and returns at once: its running time is that of starting the tone, not
   its duration. The default implementation takes a time within the bounds
   and plays nothing.

   The bounds are measured on an M5Stack CoreS3 Lite by the profile of the
   device (2026-10-14): the lower bound is the least time measured, rounded
   down, and the upper bound 1.5 times the greatest, rounded up. Beep took
   0.055 to 0.082 ms in the digital level, and its monitor reported 0.03 ms
   in the sprint start system (2026-10-15), whose task has a lower priority
   than the task of the speaker: [0, 0.15].

   On the profile m5stack-gray-radio, an M5Stack Gray with its radio
   running, the profile of the device (2026-10-19, the remote BALA2 at a
   period of 5 ms) measured Beep at 0.169 to 0.186 ms, two calls: [0.15,
   0.3]. They are not measured on other boards. The default implementation
   takes 0.15 ms, within the bounds of both boards. *)

operation Beep : nat * nat ~> unit # [0, 0.15]
default Beep _ = delay 3/20
